    "date": 1780690692,
    "caption": "819 Leaders. 9 Countries. The Largest AI Leaders Community in Central Eurasia.\n\nCongratulations to all graduates! Today, the region’s largest AI program for business leaders and executives, AI Leaders 2026, officially concluded with a high-level graduation event at alem.ai, the International Center for AI in Astana.\n\nThe graduation ceremony featured Zhaslan Madiyev @zhaslanmadiyev , Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of AI & Digital Development of Kazakhstan, Rachel Brown , Economic Strategist at OpenAI, and Asset Abdualiyev @assetabdualiyev , Founder & CEO of Silkroad Innovation Hub.\n\nThroughout the program, 819 participants from 9 countries learned from 15+ global AI experts through an applied, implementation-focused approach, with contributions from Stanford University HAI, OpenAI Academy, Lovable, CAYU, and ISSAI.\n\nThe program was organized by Silkroad Innovation Hub, with support from the Ministry of AI & Digital Development of Kazakhstan, as one of the flagship initiatives of Kazakhstan’s Year of AI.\n\nAI Leaders has established the first and largest AI community for business leaders and executives in Central Eurasia, helping drive digital transformation and AI adoption across the region.\n\nCongratulations once again to all graduates who are now part of this growing community of AI leaders.\n\nSee you at the graduation ceremonies in Tashkent, Doha, and Dushanbe!",
